CatGL:
{{Website1|webname=CatGL|url=3dengine.rbx|owner=nathan ([[Nathanielcharles0703]])|visits=1000+|purpose=API}}

CatGL (Catweb Graphics Library) is a 3d engine API created by nathanielcharles0703 that closely resembles the real OpenGL, with fragment shaders<ref>https://wikis.khronos.org/opengl/Fragment_Shader</ref>, middle to low level graphics control, and multiple libraries like CatGL Mathematics. It was made for CatBlox, a site that he is working on, and he got motivation from the Compilation Update which made scripts faster.

Unlike many 3d engines, this uses a rasterization engine<ref><nowiki>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rasterisation</nowiki></ref>. It allows for true pixel-level control, unlike point 3d engines (which one object is one point). And also, one thing, '''CatGL is completely free!'''

== Overview ==
CatGL has many libraries under it:

* CatGL Mathematics (CatGLM) - Many math functions like "glm_add"
* CatGL Wrangler and Loader Library (CatGLWLL) - Loads the CatGL functions like "glDrawTri_twd"
* CatGL Framework (CatGLFW) - Manages the viewport and camera

And these libraries also have helper libraries under them.

And as i said, CatGL closely resembles how graphics libraries work in real life. (But requires less lines). 
[[File:Screenshot 20260928 183253 Roblox.jpg|center|thumb|484x484px]]

<syntaxhighlight lang="cpp">

#include <glad/glad.h>
#include <GLFW/glfw3.h>
#include <iostream>

void framebuffer_size_callback(GLFWwindow* window, int width, int height) {
    glViewport(0, 0, width, height);
}

int main() {
    if (!glfwInit()) {
        std::cerr << "Failed to initialize GLFW" << std::endl;
        return -1;
    }

    glfwWindowHint(GLFW_CONTEXT_VERSION_MAJOR, 3);
    glfwWindowHint(GLFW_CONTEXT_VERSION_MINOR, 3);
    glfwWindowHint(GLFW_OPENGL_PROFILE, GLFW_OPENGL_CORE_PROFILE);

    // Similar to glInitVP function
    GLFWwindow* window = glfwCreateWindow(800, 600, "OpenGL Blank Window", NULL, NULL);
    if (window == NULL) {
        std::cerr << "Failed to create GLFW window" << std::endl;
        glfwTerminate();
        return -1;
    }
    glfwMakeContextCurrent(window);

    // Similar to glInitBuffer function
    glfwSetFramebufferSizeCallback(window, framebuffer_size_callback);

    if (!gladLoadGLLoader((GLADloadproc)glfwGetProcAddress)) {
        std::cerr << "Failed to initialize GLAD" << std::endl;
        return -1;
    }

    // Render loop not needed unless you are making a real time engine 
    while (!glfwWindowShouldClose(window)) {
        // Input processing is not needed here as you can trigger an event when key pressed on CatWeb
        if (glfwGetKey(window, GLFW_KEY_ESCAPE) == GLFW_PRESS) {
            glfwSetWindowShouldClose(window, true);
        }
        // Similar to glClearColor and glRefreshScreen functions
        glClearColor(0.2f, 0.3f, 0.3f, 1.0f);
        glClear(GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);

        glfwSwapBuffers(window);
        glfwPollEvents();
    }

    glfwTerminate();
    return 0;
}



</syntaxhighlight>

== Core Features ==

* Fragment Shaders for pixel level control
* Pass variables to Fragment Shaders every frame (uniforms)
* Built in projection math
* Uses multithreading, by splitting columns of pixels into their separate thread.

== Trivia ==
* The person who created this site, is also working on real OpenGL software development.
* This project was made back in September 2025
* CatGL utilizes Roblox's rich text system to bypass object limits on pixels (uses Unicode Character U+25FC and text color)

